# News admin configuration
#
# The site is published as a static bundle (GitHub Pages), so there is no server
# process that could safely hold a secret. The News admin therefore signs in
# with GitHub identity instead of a password stored in this repository:
#
#   Username: fikrado  (validated against the GitHub account that owns the token)
#   Password: a GitHub fine-grained personal access token, entered at login time
#
# Create the token at https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
# with "Contents: Read and write" limited to the fikrado2/fikrado2.github.io
# repository. The token is held in sessionStorage for the browser tab only and
# is never written into this repository.
#
# There is deliberately no ADMIN_PASSWORD value here. Anything in this file is
# committed to a public repository, so it cannot hold a real credential.
ADMIN_USERNAME=fikrado

# Optional: set this as a repository Actions secret if you later add a server
# route that needs to verify the admin offline. Never commit the real value.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME